Deadlines&Notes — feature backlog
Status: [x] shipped · [~] partial · [ ] not started
Last reviewed: 17 November 2026

Suggested build order
1. Pin/favourite + priority levels (one schema bump)
2. Checklists & subtasks
3. Rich text formatting
4. Multimedia attachments
5. Templates
6. Calendar integration
7. Daily "My Day" view
8. Collaboration (shared lists, assignment, comments)
9. AI & smart extraction

1. Note-Taking & Capture

• [~] Quick & Instant Notes: Jot down thoughts, ideas, or meeting minutes on the fly.
      Notes can be added instantly from the Notes tab; no global quick-capture
      shortcut or widget yet.
• [x] Rich Text Formatting: Apply bold, italics, underlines, highlights, and bullet points.
      Shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.9+10): the note editor has B/I/U/highlight and
      bullet buttons that wrap the selected text in lightweight inline tags
      (<b>, <i>, <u>, <m>, "- " lines). The reader renders them as selectable
      styled spans; previews and search use tag-free text. No schema or sync
      change — existing plain notes render exactly as before. Archive previews
      use the same tag-free text. 9 regression tests added in
      test/rich_text_test.dart.
      Device-verified 17 Nov 2026 (SM-N9600, 1.0.9+10): a test note saved with
      B/I/U/highlight markup plus a "- " line showed the tag-free preview
      "Bold italic under mark / • step one", the reader rendered the spans,
      search found "italic under" but not the literal "<b>". Test note
      archived and purged. The archive-preview rebuild (SHA-256 1cc31b94…)
      was superseded by 1.0.15+16, installed and device-verified on 18 Nov
      2026; the earlier installed 1.0.9+10 build was verified too.
      Interactive note checklists added 18 Nov 2026 (1.0.18+19): lines written
      as "- [ ] task" or "- [x] done" (or just "[ ] task") render as tappable
      checkboxes in the note reader, and the editor's toolbar checkbox turns
      the current line into a checklist item or ticks it. Ticking saves only
      that line's marker through the normal note save path, so no schema,
      sync, backend or dependency change is needed. Card previews and search
      show ☐/☑ instead of the raw markers. Old handwritten "[  ]" and "[v]"
      notes stay literal. 7 regression tests added in
      test/note_checklist_test.dart; flutter analyze clean and all 169 tests
      pass. Installed 18 Nov 2026 as 1.0.18+19 (SHA-256 0a881f63…) and
      device-verified (SM-N9600): the toolbar checkbox turned "Buy milk" into
      "- [ ] Buy milk" then ticked it; a second line became "- [ ] Pay rent";
      the saved card preview showed ☑/☐; the reader rendered two tappable
      checkboxes and tapping the second saved both as ticked. Existing "[  ]"
      and "[v]" notes stayed literal, and the locked note stayed masked. Test
      note archived and permanently deleted; baseline preserved at 3 open
      deadlines, 7 saved notes, archive 63 deadlines / 6 notes. App lock was
      still ON on relaunch (biometric prompt + PIN 2580 accepted).
      Word-style Enter continuation added 18 Nov 2026 (1.0.19+20): pressing
      Enter at the end of a checklist line inserts another unchecked "- [ ] "
      line; a bullet line inserts another "- " line. Pressing Enter on an
      empty item removes its marker and exits the list. Splitting a line
      mid-text keeps the marker on both halves. This is a text-input formatter
      on the note body, so it works with the soft keyboard too, and plain
      multi-line pastes are left untouched. 6 more tests in
      test/note_checklist_test.dart; flutter analyze clean and all 175 tests
      pass. Installed 18 Nov 2026 as 1.0.19+20 (SHA-256 7d51d5f7…) and
      device-verified (SM-N9600): Enter after "- [ ] One" produced another
      "- [ ] " line, typing "Two" + Enter produced a third item, and Enter on
      the empty item exited the list. A "- alpha" line continued with "- ",
      plain text stayed plain, and the saved card preview showed ☐ One / ☐ Two
      / Plain after / • alpha / • beta. Test note archived and permanently
      deleted; baseline preserved at 3 open deadlines, 7 saved notes, archive
      63 deadlines / 6 notes, locked note masked, app lock still ON (biometric
      prompt + PIN 2580 accepted).
• [~] Multimedia Attachments: Embed images, PDFs, audio voice memos, and scanned documents directly into notes.
      Built 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.10+11): the note editor's "Attach file" button
      picks existing images, PDFs, audio and documents (multi-select, 50 MB
      cap) and copies them into the app's own storage. Notes show a file-count
      badge on their card and a tappable attachment list in the reader; files
      open with an installed app. Only metadata (name/MIME/kind/size/id) is
      synced with the note — the bytes stay on this device, so another device
      shows "Not downloaded on this device". DB v8 stores the metadata as JSON
      on the note row (like task checklists); Laravel migration and sync
      validation added. A sync pull keeps local file paths and never lets an
      older payload with no attachments drop them. 15 regression tests added in
      test/attachment_test.dart; flutter analyze clean and full suite passing.
      Its APK (SHA-256 4c9cc62d…) was superseded by 1.0.15+16, which was
      installed and device-verified on 18 Nov 2026. Per-release install was
      skipped while the phone was offline.
      Capturing new photos/voice memos inside the app is not in this first
      version.
• [ ] Web Clipping: Save articles or web pages straight from a browser into your notebook.
• [x] Templates: Use pre-made structures for journals, meeting agendas, or project outlines.
      Shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.11+12): the Notes menu has "Start from a
      template" with four built-in structures — journal (dated), meeting
      agenda, project outline and shopping list. Picking one opens the normal
      note editor with title/body/tag pre-filled; the user can edit freely and
      nothing is created until Save. Bodies use the existing "- " bullet
      markup so template lines render as bullets. No schema, sync or backend
      change, and no new dependencies. 6 regression tests added in
      test/template_test.dart; flutter analyze clean and full suite passing
      (132 tests). Its APK (SHA-256 f95c6e4b…) was superseded by 1.0.15+16,
      installed and device-verified on 18 Nov 2026.

2. To-Do List & Task Management

• [x] Checklists & Subtasks: Break larger projects down into smaller, manageable action steps.
      Shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.8+9): each task has an ordered checklist of
      steps (title + done) edited in the task form with add/remove/reorder and
      a checkbox. Cards show an "x/y steps" progress bar; item titles join
      search. Items are synced as part of the task (DB v7 + Laravel JSON
      column), keep stable ids across devices, and reset to undone when a
      repeating task spawns its next occurrence. 9 regression tests added.
      Device-verified 17 Nov 2026 (SM-N9600, 1.0.8+9): a test deadline saved
      with two steps showed "1/2 steps" on its card, kept both items when
      reopened, and was found by searching "Email lecturer". Archived and
      purged; after relaunch + Drive sync the archive stayed at 63 deadlines /
      6 notes. Final state: 2 open deadlines, 6 saved notes, app lock ON
      (PIN 2580, fingerprint).
• [ ] Natural Language Parsing: Type a task with a date (e.g., "Finish report Friday 5pm") to auto-schedule it.
      Dates are picked from the date/time picker.
• [x] Priority Levels & Labels: Tag tasks by urgency, context, or category (e.g., High, Medium, Low or @work, @home).
      Shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.6+7): a None/Low/Medium/High priority can be
      set in the task form and shows on the card. It is synced data and is the
      tie-breaker inside each urgency bucket. Still one free-form tag per
      item; multiple labels are not supported.
• [x] Recurring Tasks: Set habits or chores to repeat daily, weekly, or monthly.
      Daily/weekly/monthly, with month-end clamping; completing one spawns the
      next occurrence.
• [~] Kanban & List Views: Switch between standard lists, calendar layouts, or visual board columns.
      Urgency-grouped list and the new in-app month calendar; no board columns.

3. Deadlines, Calendars & Reminders

• [~] Due Dates & Start Dates: Assign strict deadlines and scheduled windows to individual tasks.
      Due date + time works; start dates are not modelled.
• [~] Calendar Integration: Sync tasks and deadlines with external calendars (like Google Calendar, Outlook, or Apple Calendar).
      Built 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.12+13): a third Calendar tab shows a Monday-first
      month grid with a coloured urgency dot and count on each day, plus an
      agenda for the selected day. Tapping an agenda row edits that deadline;
      "Deadline here" opens the task form with that day pre-filled. Everything
      comes from the local task store and uses local dates — no permissions,
      new dependencies, backend or sync/schema changes. External two-way
      calendar sync is still not implemented. 6 regression tests added in
      test/calendar_test.dart; flutter analyze clean and all 138 tests pass.
      Its APK (SHA-256 87e63fae…) was superseded by 1.0.15+16, installed and
      device-verified on 18 Nov 2026 (month grid and selected-day agenda
      checked on the phone). Fixed 18 Nov 2026 (1.0.16+17): the grid height now
      follows the screen instead of a fixed 320px, so all six weeks (42 cells)
      stay visible; the final December row was confirmed on the phone. Follow-up
      18 Nov 2026 (1.0.17+18): the event dot grew from 6px to 12px and a size
      regression test was added; the APK (SHA-256 1d57c065…) was installed and
      the booked day still shows its event cue. flutter analyze clean and all
      162 tests pass.
• [x] Reminders & Push Notifications: Receive time-based or location-based alerts so you never miss a cutoff.
      Time-based heads-up reminders with the phone's notification tone, custom
      presets, reboot restore and a daily digest. Location-based alerts are not
      implemented.
• [x] Daily Planners / "My Day" Views: Filter down a massive list into a realistic daily focus list.
      Shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.13+14): a fourth My Day tab groups open work
      into Overdue, Today and Pinned (later) sections, with no duplicates — a
      pinned overdue task stays under Overdue with a pin icon. Rows show the
      due time, countdown and tag; a checkbox completes work in place and the
      title opens the normal task editor. "Add for today" pre-fills 9 am on the
      current day. Reads the existing task store, so no schema, sync or backend
      change. 6 regression tests added in test/my_day_test.dart; flutter analyze
      clean and all 144 tests pass. Its APK (SHA-256 7d266cc6…) was superseded
      by 1.0.15+16, installed and device-verified on 18 Nov 2026 (four tabs,
      My Day grouping checked).

4. Organization & Search

• [~] Categories, Notebooks, & Tags: Group related notes and tasks into dedicated spaces or projects.
      Tags only; no notebooks or categories.
• [ ] Bi-directional Linking: Connect related notes and tasks to each other.
• [x] Powerful Search Tools: Instant keyword or tag lookup across all your text, checklists, and attachments.
      Shipped 17 Nov 2026: case-insensitive search in both tabs across task
      title/notes/tag and note title/body/tag, combinable with the tag filter.
      Checklist item titles and attachment filenames now join the search.
• [x] Pinning & Favoriting: Keep critical notes or urgent daily tasks locked to the top of your screen.
      Shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.6+7): a pin toggle on task and note cards/notes
      view moves them to a Pinned group at the top (tasks) or the top of the
      notes list. Pin is ordinary synced data. Tasks and notes get their own
      gold border + pin indicator; DB schema bumped to v6 with a Laravel
      migration for the new columns.
      Device-verified 17 Nov 2026 (SM-N9600, 1.0.6+7): task pin created a
      PINNED group and moved the card to the top with an Unpin control; note
      pin moved a bottom note to the top of the list, and unpin restored it.
      Priority High chip set on a test task showed a HIGH flag badge; test
      task archived and purged. State restored to 2 open deadlines, 6 saved
      notes, archive 63 deadlines / 6 notes; app lock still ON (PIN 2580,
      fingerprint). Note: pin/unpin refreshed updated_at on two notes, so
      their relative display order shifted slightly; no content was lost.
      Fixed 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.7+8): "Delete forever" could be undone by the next
      sync — purged rows were hard-deleted locally, then the Drive/server
      tombstone was pulled back as a recoverable ARCHIVED row (remote payloads
      carry no permanent-delete marker). Purged rows now stay locally as hidden
      tombstones, so later pulls find them and leave them alone. Regression
      tests added in test/purge_sync_test.dart.
      Device-verified 17 Nov 2026 (SM-N9600, 1.0.7+8): re-purged ZZPriorityTest
      from the archive (63), backgrounded and relaunched the app to trigger
      Drive sync, unlocked with PIN 2580, and confirmed the task stayed gone —
      archive still 63 deadlines / 6 notes, 2 open deadlines, 6 saved notes.

5. Collaboration & Sync

• [x] Cross-Device Sync: Seamlessly sync data across mobile, tablet, desktop, and web apps (via cloud services like iCloud or proprietary sync).
      Optional Google Drive appData folder or a self-hosted Laravel server;
      newest-updated-wins merge, tombstones and ETag-safe uploads.
• [~] Shared Projects & Task Assignment: Collaborate with team members, family, or study groups by sharing lists and delegating tasks.
      First slice shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.14+15): a free-text assignee (email
      or name) on each deadline, saved in the task row and carried by the normal
      Laravel sync payload. Controls appear only when server sync is configured;
      offline and Drive users see no change. No account lookup, invitations or
      shared lists yet. DB v9 plus an undeployed Laravel migration. 9 regression
      tests added in test/collaboration_test.dart.
• [~] Comments & History: Leave feedback, track changes, or view activity logs inside shared items.
      First slice shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.14+15): a discussion thread on each
      deadline, stored as JSON on the task row and synced with it. The task form
      lets you add/remove comments with an author label; the card shows a
      comment-count pill. Recurring next occurrences carry the assignee but
      start a fresh thread. No activity/audit log yet. Its APK (SHA-256
      9eab343b…) was superseded by 1.0.15+16, installed and device-verified on
      18 Nov 2026. Controls correctly absent because no server sync is
      configured on the device.

6. Security & AI Enhancements

• [x] App & Note Locking: Protect private notes or sensitive checklists with a password, PIN, or biometrics.
      Shipped 17 Nov 2026: 4-digit app PIN (salted, iterated hash in Keystore-
      backed secure storage), optional fingerprint unlock, lock-on-background,
      and FLAG_SECURE so recents and screenshots are blocked. Individual notes
      can be locked: they are masked in the list and archive, excluded from
      search results, and stay device-local across sync. Turning app lock off
      releases every note lock. Changing the PIN, locking now and disabling all
      live in Deadlines/Notes → ⋮ → App lock.
      Verified on device 17 Nov 2026 (SM-N9600, 1.0.5+6): PIN setup/confirm,
      lock-on-background, wrong-PIN rejection, biometric prompt + PIN fallback,
      Change PIN (old rejected, new accepted), Lock now, per-note lock (masked
      card, title/body/tag all absent from search, PIN re-open), and turning
      app lock off clearing note locks. Test note removed and original app-lock
      state (PIN 2580 + fingerprint) restored afterwards.
• [~] AI & Smart Extraction: Automatically transcribe meetings, extract action items from text, or suggest schedule blocks.
      First slice shipped 17 Nov 2026 (1.0.15+16): a local, on-device paste box
      in the task form. It recognises relative/ISO/slash/named dates, times,
      hashtags or "Tag:" lines and checklist markers (-, *, •, [ ], 1.), then
      pre-fills the editable title, due date, tag, notes and steps. No network,
      API key, dependency or schema/sync/backend change; nothing is saved until
      the user taps Save. 8 regression tests added in test/smart_extract_test.dart;
      flutter analyze clean and all 161 tests pass. Installed 18 Nov 2026 as
      1.0.15+16 (SHA-256 a623ef9e…) and device-verified: the paste box filled
      a test draft ("ZZSmartTest tomorrow 5pm" → title + Thu 19 Nov, 5:00 PM),
      then the draft was discarded without saving. Data baseline preserved:
      2 open deadlines, 7 saved notes, archive 63 deadlines / 5 notes; locked
      note still locked, app lock still ON (PIN 2580 + fingerprint). Meeting
      transcription and schedule suggestions are still not implemented.

